{"uid":"2a74877d7265cc5d","name":"test_run_detail_keeps_updating_through_a_long_worker_iteration","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_run_detail_keeps_updating_through_a_long_worker_iteration","historyId":"f6ece80a0d1ebe8bdaac0587e137ebfa","time":{"start":1791894704313,"stop":1791894712859,"duration":8546},"description":"Task 022 (requirement F): before this task, the engine ran a\n    0.25s background poller (`_poll_task_changes`) purely so a task-status\n    transition written mid-iteration surfaced as a live `task` event; that\n    poller is retired. This is the black-box proof that retiring it did\n    not cost the hub's run-detail view its in-step liveness during a long\n    worker iteration.\n\n    Task 064 reshaped the proof itself: the previous version sampled\n    `#logbox`/`#task-box` on a fixed real-time loop and asserted it managed\n    `>= 4` samples inside an 8s window -- a host-throughput floor, not a\n    liveness proof (a fast host could always clear it without the page ever\n    actually refreshing with new content, and a slow host could fail it\n    while the page was working perfectly). This version instead CAUSES a\n    change mid-iteration -- appending a distinguishing event straight to\n    the currently-running iteration's own transcript file, the same file\n    `#logbox` is server-rendered from on every poll (`log_merge`/\n    `log_render`, never cached) -- and asserts the page's rendered content\n    genuinely advances to reflect it (`_assert_content_advanced`), which is\n    the actual property this test exists for. The task table (`#task-box`)\n    is still checked never to blank out or revert to its empty-state\n    placeholder across the same window.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 022 (requirement F): before this task, the engine ran a<br />\n0.25s background poller (<code>_poll_task_changes</code>) purely so a task-status<br />\ntransition written mid-iteration surfaced as a live <code>task</code> event; that<br />\npoller is retired. This is the black-box proof that retiring it did<br />\nnot cost the hub's run-detail view its in-step liveness during a long<br />\nworker iteration.</p>\n<pre><code>Task 064 reshaped the proof itself: the previous version sampled\n`#logbox`/`#task-box` on a fixed real-time loop and asserted it managed\n`&gt;= 4` samples inside an 8s window -- a host-throughput floor, not a\nliveness proof (a fast host could always clear it without the page ever\nactually refreshing with new content, and a slow host could fail it\nwhile the page was working perfectly). This version instead CAUSES a\nchange mid-iteration -- appending a distinguishing event straight to\nthe currently-running iteration's own transcript file, the same file\n`#logbox` is server-rendered from on every poll (`log_merge`/\n`log_render`, never cached) -- and asserts the page's rendered content\ngenuinely advances to reflect it (`_assert_content_advanced`), which is\nthe actual property this test exists for. The task table (`#task-box`)\nis still checked never to blank out or revert to its empty-state\nplaceholder across the same window.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791894578879,"stop":1791894578879,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791894578879,"stop":1791894578879,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791894704310,"stop":1791894704311,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessag